{"title":"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Stars_and_Bars)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Stars and Bars)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Quick_Summation)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Quick Summation)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many non-<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Similar\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Similar\">similar</a> triangles have angles whose degree measures are distinct positive integers in <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Arithmetic_progression\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Arithmetic progression\">arithmetic progression</a>? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/d/bdd1cce8256c82d17e8f809e7ff76bd465c02776.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 0\\qquad\\textbf{(B) } 1\\qquad\\textbf{(C) } 59\\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 89\\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 178\\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"425\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sum of the angles of a triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/b/5cb1b41850ab676e4d1cf15c69b1609af4befbc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> degrees. For an arithmetic progression with an odd number of terms, the middle term is equal to the average of the sum of all of the terms, making it <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/2/6724e1f344bb3eb8ab3959e723d0523578fbb57c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{180}{3} = 60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"73\" height=\"37\" /> degrees. The minimum possible value for the smallest angle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and the highest possible is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/e/afe61e5b80572ad5a200a0d9cd354ce12a8c7800.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$59$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> (since the numbers are distinct), so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/6/6c64ae31b324e697d36ab230bd1f994f7b11b9d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }59}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"30\" /> possibilities.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Stars_and_Bars.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Stars_and_Bars)\">Solution 2 (Stars and Bars)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Stars and Bars)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the first angle be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, and the common difference be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The arithmetic progression can now be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/c/e0c303310c18091b3883fd0c8e1670bde0ff1251.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + (x + d) + (x + 2d) = 180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"227\" height=\"18\" />. Simplifiying, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/1/eb1d397247a9bdb966b7f7eb64f3a3f902e5dcd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + d = 60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"84\" height=\"14\" />. Now, using stars and bars, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/2/5d24fe9bb73e57a7a04aec4ba24d933dacecc6f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{61}{1} = 61$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"87\" height=\"53\" />. \nHowever, we must subtract the two cases in which either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/c/d6c68d2e207e2d8556030042c82f53fe0ec5e4b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$61 - 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/6/6c64ae31b324e697d36ab230bd1f994f7b11b9d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }59}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Quick_Summation.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Quick_Summation)\">Solution 3 (Quick Summation)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Quick Summation)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider that we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/4/65421c21cd1efa1a7d5738372c5a6200ca87e188.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+n)+(a+n+1)+(a+n+2)=180 \\Longleftrightarrow 3a+3(n+1)=180 \\Longleftrightarrow a=59-n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"661\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/1/821d5b948fd2e8a82be18042d192710914b5e819.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/a/67a8181c9d9b8253bd721b620aaabc5b01f4af96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/b/ecb74f4e3a452e3d7a2055013d81f46c666ab1dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=0,1,2,3,\\cdots, 58$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"159\" height=\"17\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/6/6c64ae31b324e697d36ab230bd1f994f7b11b9d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }59}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"30\" /> solutions.\n</p><p>~~QuantumPsiInverted\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A\">2006 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\